<!--
  Boreas themed-icon (monochrome) layer, Android 13+.

  The system discards every colour here and keeps ONLY the alpha channel, tinting it with a
  wallpaper-derived colour. So this layer is a hard-edged silhouette: no gradient, no specular,
  no drop shadow — semi-transparent effects would survive tinting as a halo.

  Geometry matches the iOS icon: 0.729 of the 72dp visible face tall (52.488 x 35.086 dp).
  Centred on the glyph's own bounding box, not on the source viewBox — the mark sits +30.31
  units right of centre in boreas-glyph.svg, and carrying that offset over would put the bbox
  corner at 33.26dp, outside the 33dp radius that every OEM mask is guaranteed to keep.
  As centred here the half-diagonal is 31.567dp.
-->
